{"parentUuid":"d622841e-2472-4164-b75c-08c4d1608888","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2334517e-9c8b-4d92-958c-3a43b8c6b6b3","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R2U9tidXyJ1DvTfeYepC2L","type":"tool_result","content":"I've searched through the provided content, which shows the `sat_parameters.proto` file from Google OR-Tools v9.15. However, I cannot find the fields you're asking about:\n\n- `shared_tree_num_workers`\n- `shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability`\n- `shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker`\n\nThe file content displayed ends around line 1000, and the footer indicates \"[View remainder of file in raw view]\" suggesting additional content exists beyond what was provided. These parameters may be located in the portion of the file not included in your excerpt.\n\nTo locate these fields, you would need to access the complete `sat_parameters.proto` file, either by:\n1. Viewing the raw file directly on GitHub\n2. Downloading the full file from the OR-Tools repository"}]},"uuid":"c70dda65-7b0a-4789-b583-1c6d360ba6e0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:23.641Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d622841e-2472-4164-b75c-08c4d1608888","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ec8c282a-6d03-4b96-a94b-e6d661b46beb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DKscShUvtXPAT531tUZc8n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree_num_workers parameter recommendation Perron\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel search problem in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"Seeding CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/lPb1FzhTMt0\"},{\"title\":\"Get nondeterministic results with different number of workers using CP-SAT; Optimal using 1 worker, Infeasible using 8 workers · Issue #3842 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3842\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT worker parameters, including insights from Laurent Perron at Google.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**General Recommendation:**\nWhen interleave_search is true, you should just set it to your number of cores, according to Laurent Perron's guidance on the OR-Tools discussion group.\n\n**Important Context:**\nBy default, CP-SAT leverages all available cores (including hyperthreading). However, this should usually be lower than your number of available cpus + hyperthread in your machine.\n\n**Practical Considerations:**\nDecreasing the number of search workers can actually improve the runtime for some problems. Additionally, you usually want the batch size to be around twice the number of workers, so that you have a good utilization of your core if some chunks are fast to be completed (when using interleave_search).\n\nThe search results indicate that while the default behavior uses all available cores, the optimal number of workers is problem-dependent, and there isn't a one-size-fits-all recommendation. Testing with different worker counts is recommended to find the best performance for your specific problem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1653d182-d6a8-482c-a29c-5acf31c082b7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:25.404Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ec8c282a-6d03-4b96-a94b-e6d661b46beb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1653d182-d6a8-482c-a29c-5acf31c082b7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LMJimXmFVkQaeZ4F7d8kah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W6TyJ3znP1shY77MEw54pt","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/or-tools/v9.15/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find ALL fields containing \"shared_tree\" in their name. For each, quote the full comment block above the field and the field declaration line itself. Include shared_tree_num_workers, shared_tree_worker_objective_split_probability, shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker, shared_tree_split_strategy, shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker. Quote verbatim, do not paraphrase."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":22117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1782,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2FiDBkwaM1tmchY6SN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"632f7a88-36e9-4ff4-adb3-466288184269","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:31.173Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"632f7a88-36e9-4ff4-adb3-466288184269","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LMJimXmFVkQaeZ4F7d8kah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C7SHdsC2xkp5FxrjkGBXzy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html","prompt":"Find any mention of \"shared_tree_num_workers\" or \"shared tree\" workers. Quote all recommendations on how many shared tree workers to use, formulas, and the relationship to num_search_workers. Also find general guidance on num_workers / num_search_workers tuning."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":22117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1782,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":67,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2FiDBkwaM1tmchY6SN","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"97e3f1f0-6979-4f42-ae65-bd47f3ee2368","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:32.663Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"97e3f1f0-6979-4f42-ae65-bd47f3ee2368","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7SHdsC2xkp5FxrjkGBXzy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Search Results for \"shared_tree_num_workers\" and Related Guidance\n\nBased on my review of the provided web page content, I found **no mentions** of:\n- \"shared_tree_num_workers\"\n- \"shared tree\" workers\n- Formulas relating shared tree workers to search workers\n- Specific recommendations on shared tree worker counts\n\n## General num_workers Guidance Found\n\nThe document does provide general tuning recommendations for `num_workers`:\n\n**Default behavior:** \"By default, CP-SAT leverages all available cores (including hyperthreading).\"\n\n**Manual reduction suggestion:** \"For many models, you can boost performance by manually reducing the number of workers to match the number of physical cores, or even fewer. This can be beneficial for several reasons: it allows the remaining workers to run at a higher frequency, provides more memory bandwidth, and reduces potential interference between workers.\"\n\n**Important caveat:** The document notes that reducing workers \"might also decrease the overall chance of one of them making progress, as there are fewer directions being explored simultaneously.\"\n\nThe primer appears to focus on the portfolio-based parallelization strategy rather than shared-tree approaches used in some other solvers."}]},"uuid":"5b3622fb-9c1b-4b59-a771-481928eaf04c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:38.549Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"97e3f1f0-6979-4f42-ae65-bd47f3ee2368","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"632f7a88-36e9-4ff4-adb3-466288184269","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W6TyJ3znP1shY77MEw54pt","type":"tool_result","content":"# Fields Containing \"shared_tree\" in SatParameters\n\n## 1. shared_tree_num_workers\n```\n// Enables shared tree search.\n// If positive, start this many complete worker threads to explore a shared\n// search tree. These workers communicate objective bounds and simple decision\n// nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree, and will avoid exploring\n// the same subtrees as one another.\n// Specifying a negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate\n// number of shared tree workeres based on the total number of workers.\noptional int32 shared_tree_num_workers = 235 [default = -1];\n```\n\n## 2. use_shared_tree_search\n```\n// Set on shared subtree workers. Users should not set this directly.\noptional bool use_shared_tree_search = 236 [default = false];\n```\n\n## 3. shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree\n```\n// Minimum restarts before a worker will replace a subtree\n// that looks \"bad\" based on the average LBD of learned clauses.\noptional int32 shared_tree_worker_min_restarts_per_subtree = 282\n    [default = 1];\n```\n\n## 4. shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing\n```\n// If true, workers share more of the information from their local trail.\n// Specifically, literals implied by the shared tree decisions.\noptional bool shared_tree_worker_enable_trail_sharing = 295 [default = true];\n```\n\n## 5. shared_tree_worker_enable_phase_sharing\n```\n// If true, shared tree workers share their target phase when returning an\n// assigned subtree for the next worker to use.\noptional bool shared_tree_worker_enable_phase_sharing = 304 [default = true];\n```\n\n## 6. shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker\n```\n// How many open leaf nodes should the shared tree maintain per worker.\noptional double shared_tree_open_leaves_per_worker = 281 [default = 2.0];\n```\n\n## 7. shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker\n```\n// In order to limit total shared memory and communication overhead, limit the\n// total number of nodes that may be generated in the shared tree. If the\n// shared tree runs out of unassigned leaves, workers act as portfolio\n// workers. Note: this limit includes interior nodes, not just leaves.\noptional int32 shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker = 238 [default = 10000];\n```\n\n## 8. shared_tree_split_strategy\n```\nenum SharedTreeSplitStrategy {\n  // Uses the default strategy, currently equivalent to\n  // SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY.\n  SPLIT_STRATEGY_AUTO = 0;\n  // Only accept splits if the node to be split's depth+discrepancy is minimal\n  // for the desired number of leaves.\n  // The preferred child for discrepancy calculation is the one with the\n  // lowest objective lower bound or the original branch direction if the\n  // bounds are equal. This rule allows twice as many workers to work in the\n  // preferred subtree as non-preferred.\n  SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY = 1;\n  // Only split nodes with an objective lb equal to the global lb. If there is\n  // no objective, this is equivalent to SPLIT_STRATEGY_FIRST_PROPOSAL.\n  SPLIT_STRATEGY_OBJECTIVE_LB = 2;\n  // Attempt to keep the shared tree balanced.\n  SPLIT_STRATEGY_BALANCED_TREE = 3;\n  // Workers race to split their subtree, the winner's proposal is accepted.\n  SPLIT_STRATEGY_FIRST_PROPOSAL = 4;\n}\noptional SharedTreeSplitStrategy shared_tree_split_strategy = 239\n    [default = SPLIT_STRATEGY_AUTO];\n```\n\n## 9. shared_tree_balance_tolerance\n```\n// How much deeper compared to the ideal max depth of the tree is considered\n// \"balanced\" enough to still accept a split. Without such a tolerance,\n// sometimes the tree can only be split by a single worker, and they may not\n// generate a split for some time. In contrast, with a tolerance of 1, at\n// least half of all workers should be able to split the tree as soon as a\n// split becomes required. This only has an effect on\n// SPLIT_STRATEGY_BALANCED_TREE and SPLIT_STRATEGY_DISCREPANCY.\noptional int32 shared_tree_balance_tolerance = 305 [default = 1];\n```\n\n## 10. shared_tree_split_min_dtime\n```\n// How much dtime a worker will wait between proposing splits.\n// This limits the contention in splitting the shared tree, and also reduces\n// the number of too-easy subtrees that are generates.\noptional double shared_tree_split_min_dtime = 328 [default = 0.1];\n```"}]},"uuid":"f29f9b4f-777b-4e2c-a07f-7192f44a9a71","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:45.320Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"632f7a88-36e9-4ff4-adb3-466288184269","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
