{"parentUuid":"c61475f6-e7a8-41aa-b8b5-0bd45dd99c83","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KdB2MhC4yyW534zjXV1Rch","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"or-tools cpsat \"shared_tree_num_workers\" heuristic formula source code num_workers\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"Seeding CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/lPb1FzhTMt0\"},{\"title\":\"trying to solve huge mode on CP-Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the `shared_tree_num_workers` parameter in OR-Tools CP-SAT:\n\nA negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate number of shared tree workers based on the total number of workers. This indicates that when `shared_tree_num_workers` is set to a negative value (the default is -1), the solver automatically determines the number of shared tree workers using an internal heuristic formula.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the specific heuristic formula or the exact source code implementation details for how this calculation is performed. The parameter is defined in the `sat_parameters.proto` file, but users should not set this directly.\n\nTo find the actual heuristic formula and implementation in the source code, you would need to look at the OR-Tools repository's C++ implementation files, particularly in the CP-SAT solver's worker initialization code where this parameter is computed based on the total number of workers (`num_workers`).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d0eef3f5-0fb3-4108-a8dd-5f88d4db5c4b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:55.400Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c61475f6-e7a8-41aa-b8b5-0bd45dd99c83","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1fe7ebaf-6818-4602-9e7a-9266794da92d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019b27HbmsWcpT1ugTQazUvR","type":"tool_result","content":"I cannot find the specific code or formula you're asking about in the provided web page content. The page shows a GitHub code search interface for the query \"repo:google/or-tools shared_tree_num_workers,\" but it requires users to sign in before viewing actual search results.\n\nTo locate the formula for computing shared tree workers when `shared_tree_num_workers < 0`, you would need to:\n\n1. Sign into GitHub\n2. Navigate to the google/or-tools repository\n3. Search for files containing `shared_tree_num_workers` and `num_search_workers`\n4. Review the source code directly\n\nWithout access to the actual search results or code files, I cannot provide the specific formula you're requesting."}]},"uuid":"79229b47-f0f7-4991-8a83-1920262d45d9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:47:55.757Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1fe7ebaf-6818-4602-9e7a-9266794da92d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"26385e35-687e-4b1d-869b-2ae19ca9c6a6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NBu3sytgybY56Uj4K9zvmV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Parallel Search in CP-SAT: Worker Configuration\n\nBased on the discussion thread, there is **no mention of `shared_tree_num_workers` or shared tree search** in the provided content.\n\n## Recommendations from Laurent Perron\n\nThe only explicit recommendation regarding worker configuration comes from Laurent Perron:\n\n> \"For best performance, I would use 8 threads. To have speedup, you do need 8 cores, otherwise other threads will slow down the lucky one that will find a good solution.\"\n\n## Key Points\n\n1. **Non-deterministic behavior**: The developer noted that \"parallel search is not deterministic\" and acknowledged future plans to change this, though optimization gains would be sacrificed.\n\n2. **Hardware dependency**: Performance improvements require sufficient CPU cores matching the thread count—using more threads than available cores can degrade performance.\n\n3. **Variable results**: Even with proper configuration, parallel search introduces inherent variability in execution time due to its probabilistic nature, as evidenced by the user's test results (16-21 seconds across runs).\n\nThe discussion focuses on the `num_search_workers` parameter for enabling multiple threads, but does not address shared tree approaches or more granular worker configuration options."}]},"uuid":"09ccd697-2581-4f7c-abe6-b7524cef590a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:48:00.836Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"26385e35-687e-4b1d-869b-2ae19ca9c6a6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
