{"parentUuid":"adaaab5a-bef7-45b4-a60a-015d8de955f0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01LVLr7B7aZ9SNZsjinNeALt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VnAPDnuYvgBb3oHMhWFKTj","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"shared_tree_num_workers\" cp-sat issue github"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1426,"cache_read_input_tokens":32224,"output_tokens":292,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1426},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":292,"cache_read_input_tokens":32224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1426,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2LDdcPpP5eTfsfm67R","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"acac6b45-2c43-4f6e-a9b1-169b6ad6f057","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:48:31.503Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"adaaab5a-bef7-45b4-a60a-015d8de955f0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BUxLZBjH7nHqbu9wNmqH2s","type":"tool_result","content":"      if (status == SatSolver::INFEASIBLE) {\n        shared_response_manager->NotifyThatImprovingProblemIsInfeasible(\n            model->Name());\n        break;\n      }\n      if (status == SatSolver::FEASIBLE) {\n        solution_observer();\n      } else {\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n  } else if (!model_proto.has_objective()) {\n    while (true) {\n      if (parameters.use_shared_tree_search()) {\n        auto* subtree_worker = model->GetOrCreate<SharedTreeWorker>();\n        status = subtree_worker->Search(solution_observer);\n      } else {\n        status = ResetAndSolveIntegerProblem(\n            mapping.Literals(model_proto.assumptions()), model);\n      }\n      if (status != SatSolver::Status::FEASIBLE) break;\n      solution_observer();\n      if (!parameters.enumerate_all_solutions()) break;\n      model->Add(ExcludeCurrentSolutionAndBacktrack());\n    }\n    if (status == SatSolver::INFEASIBLE) {\n      shared_response_manager->NotifyThatImprovingProblemIsInfeasible(\n          model->Name());\n    }\n    if (status == SatSolver::ASSUMPTIONS_UNSAT) {\n      shared_response_manager->NotifyThatImprovingProblemIsInfeasible(\n          model->Name());\n\n      // Extract a good subset of assumptions and add it to the response.\n      auto* time_limit = model->GetOrCreate<TimeLimit>();\n      auto* sat_solver = model->GetOrCreate<SatSolver>();\n      std::vector<Literal> core = sat_solver->GetLastIncompatibleDecisions();\n      MinimizeCoreWithPropagation(time_limit, sat_solver, &core);\n      std::vector<int> core_in_proto_format;\n      for (const Literal l : core) {\n        core_in_proto_format.push_back(\n            mapping.GetProtoVariableFromBooleanVariable(l.Variable()));\n        if (!l.IsPositive()) {\n          core_in_proto_format.back() = NegatedRef(core_in_proto_format.back());\n        }\n      }\n      shared_response_manager->AddUnsatCore(core_in_proto_format);\n    }\n  } else {\n    // Optimization problem.\n    const auto& objective = *model->GetOrCreate<ObjectiveDefinition>();\n    const IntegerVariable objective_var = objective.objective_var;\n    CHECK_NE(objective_var, kNoIntegerVariable);\n\n    if (parameters.optimize_with_lb_tree_search()) {\n      auto* search = model->GetOrCreate<LbTreeSearch>();\n      status = search->Search(solution_observer);\n    } else if (parameters.optimize_with_core()) {\n      // TODO(user): This doesn't work with splitting in chunk for now. It\n      // shouldn't be too hard to fix.\n      if (parameters.optimize_with_max_hs()) {\n        status = model->Mutable<HittingSetOptimizer>()->Optimize();\n      } else {\n        status = model->Mutable<CoreBasedOptimizer>()->Optimize();\n      }\n    } else if (parameters.use_shared_tree_search()) {\n      auto* subtree_worker = model->GetOrCreate<SharedTreeWorker>();\n      status = subtree_worker->Search(solution_observer);\n    } else {\n      // TODO(user): This parameter breaks the splitting in chunk of a Solve().\n      // It should probably be moved into another SubSolver altogether.\n      if (parameters.binary_search_num_conflicts() >= 0) {\n        RestrictObjectiveDomainWithBinarySearch(objective_var,\n                                                solution_observer, model);\n      }\n      status = MinimizeIntegerVariableWithLinearScanAndLazyEncoding(\n          objective_var, solution_observer, model);\n    }\n\n    // The search is done in both case.\n    //","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"81528308-93ed-47e1-9576-ca0513a5eb83","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:48:32.477Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"adaaab5a-bef7-45b4-a60a-015d8de955f0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"acac6b45-2c43-4f6e-a9b1-169b6ad6f057","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VnAPDnuYvgBb3oHMhWFKTj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"shared_tree_num_workers\" cp-sat issue github\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"Get nondeterministic results with different number of workers using CP-SAT; Optimal using 1 worker, Infeasible using 8 workers · Issue #3842 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3842\"},{\"title\":\"Segmentation fault running CP-SAT with 1 worker using free-search in 9.11 · Issue #4412 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4412\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Higher num_search_workers value increases the resolution time · Issue #1921 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1921\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT model that most of the time solved to optimality, but in rare cases it is determined to be infeasible · Issue #4839 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4839\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: not all threads are used, why? · Issue #2399 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2399\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT LNS threads · Issue #1314 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1314\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several GitHub issues related to CP-SAT and the `num_workers` parameter (which was previously called `num_search_workers`). Here are the key findings:\n\n## Issues Found\n\n**Issue #3662** - CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. The report shows that with num_workers=5 the solver found the optimal solution in less than 1 second, while with num_workers=4 the solver spent whole 60 seconds and only returned a feasible solution. Interestingly, with num_workers=1,2,3 the solver only returned a feasible solution like num_workers=4 case.\n\n**Issue #3590** - Reports nondeterministic results, where users experienced issues setting `num_workers` to 1 for deterministic testing.\n\n**Issue #3842** - Non-deterministic results using different number of workers, with optimal solution found when solver.parameters.num_search_workers = 1 and infeasible solution when solver.parameters.num_search_workers = 8.\n\n**Issue #1921** - Documents a performance degradation where higher worker counts actually increased resolution time on a 32-core machine.\n\nThe search results reveal that the `num_workers` parameter in CP-SAT has various performance and determinism issues, particularly with different worker counts producing different solution qualities or affecting the time to prove optimality.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8db099f0-a96d-4438-baa8-765ed30cd4a1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:48:39.693Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"acac6b45-2c43-4f6e-a9b1-169b6ad6f057","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
