{"parentUuid":"02c1226d-56db-4722-a448-24d4f068cecc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cd88cfb2-315e-4855-9cc2-0d18adaa8e39","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fs3RkRYD1Ykn3x6dGT4xR7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Response\n\nI cannot provide the requested information. The webpage content provided does not contain any discussion of `shared_tree`, `shared_tree_num_workers`, or the relationship between `num_workers` and parallel search strategies.\n\nThe GitHub issue #1314 only documents a user's question about CP-SAT's `lns_num_threads` parameter not appearing to use multiple threads when monitoring processes. There is no substantive discussion or resolution visible in the provided content that addresses the specific terms you've asked me to quote.\n\nTo find information on those topics, you would need to review additional documentation or discussion threads related to the CP-SAT solver's parallelization features."}]},"uuid":"16714ca1-44c6-4508-abf9-b649236de907","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:49:27.227Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02c1226d-56db-4722-a448-24d4f068cecc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"51478296-1cf8-4a28-82c1-dc148fdb8f56","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b30ea096-1ee2-405a-8976-12164b1b74e7","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ATPjHByvW3i7heAKjqetJV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"shared_tree\" CP-SAT 9.15 OR 9.14 benchmark performance optimization\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization of Timed Petri Nets using CP-SAT - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405896324000946\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"arXiv:2504.14506v1 [math.OC] 20 Apr 2025 On Solving the Set Covering Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.14506\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"📈 #76 Optimizing with Google OR-Tools: strategies and insights from three years of real-world experience\",\"url\":\"https://www.feasible.club/p/76-optimizing-with-google-or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"Selecting SAT Encodings for Pseudo-Boolean and Linear Integer Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol235-cp2022/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38.pdf\"}]\n\nI searched for information about \"shared_tree\" in CP-SAT with performance benchmarks, but the results don't contain specific information about a \"shared_tree\" parameter or feature in CP-SAT versions 9.15 or 9.14.\n\nHowever, based on the search results, I can provide some context about CP-SAT performance optimization:\n\nCP-SAT uses portfolio parallelism where multiple search strategies run in parallel, each with different heuristics, restart strategies, and randomization, with solutions found by any worker shared with all workers. CP-SAT includes Large-Neighborhood Search and automatic restarts as part of its optimization strategy.\n\nTo get more specific information about \"shared_tree\" and benchmark comparisons between versions 9.15 and 9.14, I would recommend:\n\n1. Checking the official Google OR-Tools GitHub repository and release notes for versions 9.14 and 9.15\n2. Reviewing the CP-SAT documentation or research papers published by the Google OR-Tools team\n3. Looking at the OR-Tools issue tracker for discussions about this feature\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about CP-SAT versions 9.14 and 9.15 release notes, or do you have additional context about what \"shared_tree\" refers to?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1d0b9a2b-189b-412c-a631-d8dfcb05b5ff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:49:29.349Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51478296-1cf8-4a28-82c1-dc148fdb8f56","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"addaffc8-c6b8-4ba4-b2f6-c5592e71a53f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b30ea096-1ee2-405a-8976-12164b1b74e7","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01StCvTfm1ubmo3KpX4mBYV9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"shared tree search\" Perron CP-SAT 2023 OR 2024 paper presentation talk\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver (Invited Talk) - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3\"},{\"title\":\"The CP-SAT-LP Solver Laurent Perron # Google, Paris, France Frédéric Didier #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/380927615_ViolationLS_Constraint-Based_Local_Search_in_CP-SAT\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/73/4963.html\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_16\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Bench: Evaluating Large Language Models for Constraint Modelling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.06052v1\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_16\"},{\"title\":\"The Work Task Variation Problem\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.24\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about Laurent Perron and CP-SAT work from 2023-2024:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\nLaurent Perron presented \"The CP-SAT-LP Solver\" as an invited talk at the 29th International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2023). The CP-SAT-LP solver is developed by the Operations Research team at Google and is part of the OR-Tools open-source optimization suite.\n\nA key feature of CP-SAT-LP is that the continuous sharing of information between workers has produced massive speedups when running multiple workers in parallel.\n\nAdditionally, in 2024, Toby O. Davies, Frédéric Didier, and Laurent Perron published \"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT\" at CPAIOR 2024.\n\n**Note:** While my search results show extensive work on CP-SAT and parallel execution with information sharing between workers, I did not find a specific paper or presentation explicitly titled \"shared tree search\" in the 2023-2024 timeframe. The results do emphasize the importance of shared information between parallel workers in CP-SAT's architecture, which may be what you're referring to. If you need more specific information about \"shared tree search,\" you might want to check conference proceedings directly or search for more specific technical documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7055042f-8d56-4650-b330-d9391f2be3c6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:49:31.322Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"addaffc8-c6b8-4ba4-b2f6-c5592e71a53f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7055042f-8d56-4650-b330-d9391f2be3c6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016FDLgRQN2S2PfmEJyoFVHQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T12T99iBifgh7eixhHS1e4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol280-cp2023/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3.pdf","prompt":"Search for any discussion of \"shared tree\", \"shared_tree\", or LBBD in this CP-SAT-LP Solver paper. Quote any sentences mentioning shared tree search, parallel tree-splitting, or the recommended number of shared tree workers. Also note what the paper says about num_search_workers / num_workers tuning."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3362,"cache_read_input_tokens":43091,"output_tokens":262,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3362},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":262,"cache_read_input_tokens":43091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3362,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2QyNW6iTXfkY3YEm6S","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"76fa6c04-077e-407e-8015-ea3d388da7f4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:49:36.551Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"76fa6c04-077e-407e-8015-ea3d388da7f4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b30ea096-1ee2-405a-8976-12164b1b74e7","agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T12T99iBifgh7eixhHS1e4","type":"tool_result","content":"I've reviewed the provided PDF content, which appears to be a research paper on CP-SAT-LP Solver. However, the document content is heavily compressed and encoded (it's a PDF in FlateDecode format), making it impossible to reliably extract and search for specific text about \"shared tree,\" \"shared_tree,\" LBBD, or related parallel search terminology.\n\nTo properly address your request, I would need either:\n1. A plain text version of the paper\n2. An uncompressed PDF that allows text extraction\n3. The paper's title and publication details so I can reference the actual content\n\nWithout access to readable text, I cannot provide accurate quotations or information about the paper's discussion of shared tree search, parallel tree-splitting strategies, or worker configuration recommendations.\n\nIf you can provide the text content or a more accessible format, I'd be happy to search for those specific topics and provide the requested information with proper quotation marks and character limits.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 323.5KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778194179106-ux54kf.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"9f23f312-b413-408c-a5a1-48e8058c8baa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:49:42.865Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"76fa6c04-077e-407e-8015-ea3d388da7f4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9f23f312-b413-408c-a5a1-48e8058c8baa","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"af3d797751cb8bbb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ab3YgAqMEB7Xm8HUezsaZT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我已经有了足够证据。最后核对一个 8-worker 边界情况：当 `num_workers=8` 时，公式 `(8-16)/2 = -4`（objective）或 `(8-8)*3/4 = 0`（无 objective），都是 `≤ 4`，所以**默认情况下 8 worker + objective 模式下 shared_tree 是 0（disabled）**——这正好对上 R5 的观测。\n\n总结报告：\n\n---\n\n# OR-Tools 9.15 CP-SAT `shared_tree_num_workers` 调研结论\n\n## 1. 官方公式（实锤）\n\n`sat_parameters.proto` 字段 235，default = -1。注释：\n\n> \"If positive, start this many complete worker threads to explore a shared search tree... Specifying a negative number uses a heuristic to select an appropriate number of shared tree workers based on the total number of workers.\"\n\nheuristic 实际公式在 `ortools/sat/cp_model_solver_helpers.cc:2206-2218`（v9.15 tag）：\n\n```cpp\nif (params->shared_tree_num_workers() == -1) {\n  int num_shared_tree_workers = 0;\n  if (model_proto.has_objective() ||\n      model_proto.has_floating_point_objective()) {\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (params->num_workers() - 16) / 2;\n  } else {\n    num_shared_tree_workers = (params->num_workers() - 8) * 3 / 4;\n  }\n  if (num_shared_tree_workers > 4) {\n    params->set_shared_tree_num_workers(num_shared_tree_workers);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**关键观察**：还有一个 **`> 4` 阈值**——auto 模式下，公式算出来 ≤4 时**不写回**，参数保留 -1，下游再用 `std::max(0, params.shared_tree_num_workers())` 归零（见 `work_assignment.cc:266`），最终生效 0。这就是为什么 R5 在 8 worker + objective 模式下解出 0 disabled——因为 `(8-16)/2 = -4 < 4`。\n\n| num_workers | objective 模式 auto 值 | 无 objective auto 值 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 4 | -6 → 0 | -3 → 0 |\n| 8 | -4 → 0 | 0 → 0 |\n| 16 | 0 → 0 | 6 → 6 |\n| 24 | 4 → **0**（不 > 4，仍归零）| 12 → 12 |\n| 32 | 8 → 8 | 18 → 18 |\n\n## 2. 是否从 num_workers 中扣\n\n**扣**，不是叠加。`cp_model_solver.cc:1810-1828`：先创建 `num_shared_tree_workers` 个 shared_tree FullProblemSolver 实例，再调用 `GetFullWorkerParameters(..., num_already_present=full_worker_subsolvers.size(), ...)`，后者用 `num_workers - num_already_present` 计算剩余 portfolio 名额（`cp_model_search.cc:1005`）。8 worker 里塞 4 个 shared_tree，就只剩 4 个跑 portfolio。\n\n## 3. 边界\n\n- `shared_tree_num_workers >= 2` 才会真启用（`cp_model_solver.cc:1813`：`if (num_shared_tree_workers >= 2 && ...)`），单个 shared_tree worker 没意义、被忽略\n- 设为 1 → 静默忽略\n- 设大于 num_workers → 不会报错，但 portfolio 名额被压到 0，整个 solver 退化成纯 shared_tree 探索（不推荐）\n- assumptions 非空时整段 shared_tree 不启用\n\n## 4. max problem vs UNSAT\n\n公式本身就把 objective vs no-objective 分两支：**有 objective 时阈值显著更高**（要 num_workers ≥ 26 才开 5 个 shared_tree worker；no-objective 只需 ≥ 16）。Google 团队的判断是 shared tree 对 SAT/可行性证明（含 UNSAT 子树）收益更高，对 max/min 优化收益要在更高并行度下才划算。我们是 max_lex(area, min_side) 优化问题——属于\"有 objective\"分支，**8 worker 远低于阈值**。\n\n## 5. 实证文献\n\n- Perron & Didier, \"The CP-SAT-LP Solver\"（CP 2023, LIPIcs vol 280, paper 3）是当时的旗舰综述，但 PDF 文本提取失败，我无法引用具体段落。论文整体强调 portfolio + 信息共享带来 massive speedup，未公开 shared_tree 的独立 benchmark\n- 公开 issue/讨论组里没人晒过 shared_tree_num_workers 调参的对比数据\n- Perron 在 or-tools-discuss 反复强调的还是 num_workers ≈ 物理核数\n\n## 6. 推荐值\n\n8 worker master + max_lex objective + benders LBBD 上下文：\n\n**对 8 worker master 推荐 shared_tree_num_workers = 0（显式禁用），依据 = 官方 auto 公式 `(num_workers-16)/2 = -4` 在该规模下本就归零；shared_tree workers 从 num_workers 中扣除而非叠加，强行设 ≥2 会把 portfolio 压到 6 个、损失多样性；Google 团队把 objective 分支的隐式启用阈值定在 num_workers ≥ 26 是有理由的——max problem 上小并行度时 shared tree 切分开销 > 收益。要么保持 explicit 0、要么把 master 升到 ≥16 worker 才考虑 ≥2。**\n\n如果未来 master 扩到 16 worker，按公式应设 = 0（仍 -4 → 归零）；24 worker 设 = 0（4 → 不过阈值）；32 worker 才有意义、推荐 = 8（与 auto 一致）。\n\n## Sources\n- [or-tools v9.15 sat_parameters.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [cp_model_solver_helpers.cc heuristic at line 2206](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver_helpers.cc)\n- [cp_model_search.cc num_already_present at line 1005](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc)\n- [cp_model_solver.cc shared_tree allocation at 1810](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc)\n- [work_assignment.cc num_workers_ clamp](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/v9.15/ortools/sat/work_assignment.cc)\n- [Perron & Didier, The CP-SAT-LP Solver, CP 2023](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2023.3)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - Parameters chapter](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [or-tools-discuss: Parallel search problem](https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/i3TF_Szuz_k)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":46453,"output_tokens":2543,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":676},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2543,"cache_read_input_tokens":46453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":676,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Cap2RpnMCwozRnZJUXRvf","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc4667c1-c98d-4461-a137-c67391a74858","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:50:25.310Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
